    ('D32', 'High', 'Lab timing', 'Section G', 'The CRF does not say which result to record when a patient has several during the admission (first, worst, or closest to the interview), or how long after admission results may be collected. Scores depend on it, and results arrive later than the interview.', 'Record the first result after admission, with the sample date (G0, added). Results more than 7 days before admission are flagged.', 'PI + supervisor', '', 'Open'),
    ('D04', 'High', 'Child-Pugh', 'Section I', 'Section I asks the interviewer to tick bilirubin, albumin, INR and encephalopathy points by hand, although Sections D and G already hold the values. Hand scoring adds errors, and the CRF has no cut-offs printed. Ascites grade (None/Mild/Moderate-Severe) is not in Section D, which only has Present/Absent.', 'Points for bilirubin, albumin, INR and encephalopathy are calculated (standard cut-offs). Only the ascites grade (I4) is entered.', 'PI', 'CRF v0.2: Section I removed; the system calculates Child-Pugh. Ascites points now come from the F7a grade (see D36).', 'Answered'),
