    ('D20', 'High', 'Transplant eligibility', 'Section K', 'K1 (Child-Pugh C) and K2 (MELD-Na >= 15) can be calculated. K7 "accepted criteria" is not defined (any one indication? a combination? a reference guideline?). K6 Milan criteria needs tumour number and size, which the CRF does not collect.', "K1 and K2 calculated. K7 entered as the assessor's judgement. Define K7 and decide whether to add HCC number and largest size (Milan: 1 lesion <= 5 cm, or up to 3 lesions <= 3 cm, no vascular invasion).", 'PI + supervisor', 'CRF v0.2: K1 (Child-Pugh C), K2 (MELD-Na), K6 (Milan) and K7 (meets criteria) removed; HCC lesion details added to G26. Replaced by D37 (definition of the outcome) and D40 (Milan).', 'Answered'),
    ('D02', 'High', 'Eligibility', 'No CRF item', 'The CRF has no inclusion/exclusion checklist or consent record (date of consent, who consented: patient or relative, e.g. for encephalopathy). The proposal was not available.', 'Not built yet. Add an eligibility and consent section when the proposal arrives.', 'PI', '', 'Open'),
    ('D21', 'High', 'Dates', 'H, L1', 'There is no admission date or discharge/death date, so length of stay (L1) cannot be checked, and lab timing cannot be judged. Cause and date of death are not collected.', 'Admission date (H5) and discharge/death date (L3) added; L1 is checked against them. Decide whether to add cause of death.', 'PI', '', 'Open'),
    ('D36', 'High', 'Child-Pugh', 'F7a', 'CRF v0.2 grades ascites as Moderate or Severe only. Child-Pugh uses None / Mild (slight, or controlled with diuretics) = 2 / Moderate-severe (tense or refractory) = 3, so the grades do not map directly.', 'For now: Absent = 1, Moderate = 2, Severe = 3 points. Either confirm, or print the Child-Pugh grades (None / Mild / Moderate-severe) on the CRF.', 'PI + supervisor', '', 'Open'),
