    ('D35', 'Medium', 'MRN', 'H1a', 'The hospital number is recorded for every patient and is required before a participant can be registered, but it is not printed on the CRF. The MNH system shows both an MR number (one per patient) and an IP number (one per admission).', 'Required and unique; letters, digits, "-", "/" and "." accepted, stored in capitals. Add an "MRN" line to the CRF header.', 'PI', 'Use the MRN (medical record number), which stays the same across admissions. Decided by the study team, 8 Nov 2026.', 'Answered'),
